 of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. In 2025, March to April hit 182% of normal on the middle while January to February sat at 53%. In 2026 so far, June to July is at 177% of normal on the middle. A preliminary estimate from NOAA rain puts August to September 2026 at 46.5 on grid 19336.</p>"}
